  faqs: [
    { question: "How do I find IB and IGCSE tutors in Kurnool?", answer: "Write to us with your child's starting point, at Monte International and wanting more depth, a private candidate, a boarder, or adding subjects beside a State Board or CBSE place, plus the programme and level. Kurnool's own thin school base means we hunt for fit and recent teaching history over anything to do with where a tutor lives. A free lesson happens before any decision, and a different tutor is one message away if the first pairing misses." },
    { question: "Do you offer IGCSE home tutors in Kurnool for Cambridge and Edexcel?", answer: "Both boards are covered, and it's online home tuition throughout rather than someone arriving at the house. A Cambridge student gets matched down to the code and tier, say Mathematics 0580 Extended, while an Edexcel student is matched by specification and by Foundation or Higher, with each one taught strictly from that board's own papers and mark schemes rather than a blend of the two." },
    { question: "Do your tutors visit homes in Kurnool?", answer: "No. A tutor arriving at the house is something we run only in Gurugram and parts of Delhi NCR; everywhere else, Kurnool included, a lesson is a live video call with a shared whiteboard doing the work a physical presence would otherwise do. It is genuine tuition delivered at home, just not by someone standing in your living room." },
    { question: "Which schools in Kurnool teach IB or IGCSE?", answer: "Monte International School in Kallur is the one school we could confirm teaching IGCSE anywhere in Kurnool city. We have not been able to confirm any school running the IB Diploma in Kurnool. Nandi Academy International School in Nandyal, roughly 60 km away and now in its own separate district, also runs IGCSE alongside CBSE, if that distance works for a family." },
    { question: "What does an IB or IGCSE tutor in Kurnool cost?", answer: "Four things move the number: which programme, which subject, how long each session runs, and whether the tutor is topping up a subject or building an entire course from nothing for a private candidate, the second being the pricier job. We put a figure in writing ahead of the trial, add nothing to it for travel since every lesson is online, and never lock a family into anything beyond a rolling, cancel-anytime review." },
    { question: "Is there a free trial class before I commit?", answer: "Yes. Your child works through a real topic from their syllabus with the tutor online, at no charge and with no obligation to continue. A short first-month plan follows the trial, and you decide from there whether to proceed, adjust it, or ask for a different tutor." },
    { question: "Can a tutor help with IB Internal Assessments in Kurnool?", answer: "Yes, within limits. A tutor helps choose a workable research question, explains what each assessment criterion actually rewards, works through realistic data collection given the limited lab or field access most Kurnool students have outside a school setting, and gives honest feedback on drafts. Writing or rewriting the assessed work itself breaches IB academic integrity rules, so that request is declined." },
    { question: "Which IB Diploma subjects can you help with in Kurnool?", answer: "Requests here cluster around a fairly predictable set: Maths, whichever of Analysis and Approaches or Applications and Interpretation a student has chosen, the three sciences, Economics, Business Management, English A and Computer Science, with Theory of Knowledge and Extended Essay guidance layered in wherever needed. If a subject you need isn't on that list, ask anyway; the actual roster is broader than what gets requested most." },
    { question: "Do you tutor IB MYP and PYP students in Kurnool, not only the Diploma?", answer: "Yes, the whole continuum is covered. A Kurnool MYP student typically needs us either during a boarding-school holiday or ahead of a Class 9 or 10 transfer, with time spent mostly on writing at the right criterion level and pushing the Personal Project journal forward. Younger PYP students get shorter, more frequent sessions built around reading confidence and the inquiry skills that eventually feed the Exhibition." },
    { question: "Is online tutoring realistic when Kurnool has almost no local IB or IGCSE school?", answer: "Given the alternative, yes. A screen-share, a stack of marked past papers and recorded explanations cover nearly everything a physical classroom would, minus the room itself, and in exchange a Kurnool family gets to pick from tutors anywhere in the country instead of the handful, at most, who might be teaching this content within city limits." },
    { question: "How are IB Gram tutors verified for Kurnool students?", answer: "Before a name reaches a family, we look at qualifications, whether they've taught this precise subject and level recently, and how they talk about marking IAs and coursework. Kurnool's thin local options mean we lean toward tutors who are comfortable owning an entire course rather than only reinforcing what a classroom already covers. Everything after that gets tested in the trial lesson, which is where a family actually decides." },
    { question: "When should my child in Kurnool start IB or IGCSE tutoring?", answer: "Right when the course begins is ideal, Grade 9 for IGCSE and the run-up to Class 11 for the Diploma, since a school would ordinarily supply the structure a private candidate has to build with a tutor instead. Coming in later isn't a lost cause; it just means narrowing down to whichever topics and past papers will move the needle most before the actual exam." },
    { question: "My child studies at a State Board or CBSE school in Kurnool. Can a tutor add IB or IGCSE subjects?", answer: "This is genuinely one of our more frequent Kurnool enquiries, precisely because it avoids an outright school change. Most of the effort goes into two things a State Board or CBSE education rarely teaches on its own: command words like 'evaluate' and 'justify', and how to actually plan a piece of coursework, all scheduled so it doesn't eat into the hours school and homework already claim." },
    { question: "Can sessions happen on weekends or after school hours in Kurnool?", answer: "They can, and mostly do; weekday evenings once school and work wind down, plus weekend mornings, are the default. Summer scheduling shifts earlier once Rayalaseema's heat peaks, and mid-January bends around Sankranti when most of Andhra Pradesh effectively pauses. A second slot ahead of an exam series is easy enough to add if the calendar allows." },
    { question: "What happens if we are not happy with the tutor in Kurnool?", answer: "Say so, plainly, and a replacement follows. Regular check-ins exist specifically to catch a poor fit before it wastes months of lessons, and our default is to swap rather than to insist a child push through with someone who isn't working. Since nothing here is a fixed-term contract, stepping away entirely is just as available as asking for someone new." },
    { question: "Do you offer Telugu or Hindi language support alongside IB or IGCSE subjects?", answer: "IB Hindi B is on offer for a student who already has some grounding in the language, and IGCSE First Language English gets matched on its own terms by board and tier rather than folded into another subject. Since Telugu-medium schooling is common background here, tell us about your child's language history upfront and it will shape who gets shortlisted." },
    { question: "Is IB Gram affiliated with Monte International School or with the IB or Cambridge?", answer: "It isn't. There's no partnership, sponsorship or reporting line between IB Gram and Monte International, any other school named on this page, or the awarding bodies themselves, the IB Organization, Cambridge International and Pearson Edexcel included. Schools come up here purely to describe what actually exists around Kurnool, and every tutor teaches to that board's genuine, published syllabus." },
  ],

